From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: jz4740: fix DMA teardown without a data request

jz4740_mmc_post_request() runs the DMA teardown path whenever the
request failed. It does not check that the request has data, and it
does not check that DMA channels were acquired. When
jz4740_mmc_acquire_dma_channels() fails, host->dma_tx/host->dma_rx
hold error pointers, so terminating the channel dereferences
ERR_PTR(-ENODEV). A failing SDIO command during probe then takes the
kernel down with an unaligned access instead of returning the error.

Only touch DMA for a data request when host->use_dma is set, and skip
invalid channels.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
@@ -399,10 +399,11 @@ static void jz4740_mmc_post_request(struct mmc_host *mmc,
 	if (data && data->host_cookie != COOKIE_UNMAPPED)
 		jz4740_mmc_dma_unmap(host, data);
 
-	if (err) {
+	if (err && host->use_dma && data && !IS_ERR(data)) {
 		struct dma_chan *chan = jz4740_mmc_get_dma_chan(host, data);
 
-		dmaengine_terminate_all(chan);
+		if (chan)
+			dmaengine_terminate_all(chan);
 	}
 }
